],{"class":529},[515,1185,656],{"class":581},[515,1187,659],{"class":529},[515,1189,901],{"class":525},[515,1191,597],{"class":529},[515,1193,591],{"class":529},[515,1195,614],{"class":525},[515,1197,670],{"class":529},[515,1199,1201,1203,1205,1207,1209],{"class":517,"line":1200},23,[515,1202,642],{"class":529},[515,1204,884],{"class":525},[515,1206,647],{"class":529},[515,1208,1147],{"class":581},[515,1210,1021],{"class":529},[515,1212,1214,1216,1218],{"class":517,"line":1213},24,[515,1215,676],{"class":632},[515,1217,679],{"class":521},[515,1219,546],{"class":529},[515,1221,1223,1225,1227,1229,1232,1234,1237,1239],{"class":517,"line":1222},25,[515,1224,687],{"class":529},[515,1226,690],{"class":632},[515,1228,693],{"class":529},[515,1230,1231],{"class":588},"Throwable",[515,1233,591],{"class":529},[515,1235,1236],{"class":525},"error",[515,1238,698],{"class":529},[515,1240,636],{"class":529},[515,1242,1244,1246,1248,1250,1253],{"class":517,"line":1243},26,[515,1245,642],{"class":529},[515,1247,884],{"class":525},[515,1249,647],{"class":529},[515,1251,1252],{"class":581},"rollBack",[515,1254,1021],{"class":529},[515,1256,1258,1261,1263,1265],{"class":517,"line":1257},27,[515,1259,1260],{"class":632},"        throw",[515,1262,591],{"class":529},[515,1264,1236],{"class":525},[515,1266,546],{"class":529},[515,1268,1270],{"class":517,"line":1269},28,[515,1271,716],{"class":529},[515,1273,1275],{"class":517,"line":1274},29,[515,1276,722],{"class":529},[493,1278,1279],{},"The second parse inside Fluent is intentional: the first verifies the event ID before deduplication; the processor still verifies every delivery it handles. Adapt the insert to your database's conflict syntax. A lock timeout or deadlock must fail the request and retry, not return success.",[493,1281,1282],{},"Queue emails, provisioning, and other external effects through an outbox committed with the billing writes. Do not send an email inside the transaction: a rollback cannot unsend it. Make outbox consumers idempotent too. Event-ID deduplication handles redelivery of one event; unique entity IDs and idempotent fulfillment rules also protect against different events for the same payment.",[493,1284,1285],{},"Deliveries can arrive out of order. Store-or-update does not prevent an older snapshot overwriting a newer one, and find-or-skip events cannot repair a missing row. Define reconciliation and stale-event handling in your driver. Persist test mode and keep test deliveries away from live access rules.",[727,1287,1289],{"id":1288},"add-application-reactions","Add application reactions",[493,1291,1292,1293,1296,1297,1300,1301,1304,1305,1308],{},"Pass ",[497,1294,1295],{},"WebhookReactionInterface"," implementations in ",[497,1298,1299],{},"Wiring(additionalWebhookReactions: [...])",". They run after built-ins and before the final event dispatch. Typed webhook events live in ",[497,1302,1303],{},"Vatly\\API\\Webhooks\\Events","; local-row-created events live in ",[497,1306,1307],{},"Vatly\\Fluent\\Events",".",[493,1310,1311,1312,1314,1315,1308],{},"Use ",[502,1313,58],{"href":203}," to test signatures, rollback, and retries. For payload fields, see the ",[502,1316,334],{"href":1317,"rel":1318},"https:\u002F\u002Fdocs.vatly.com\u002Fapi-reference",[1319],"nofollow",[1321,1322,1323],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sbssI, html code.shiki .sbssI{--shiki-light:#F76D47;--shiki-default:#F78C6C;--shiki-dark:#F78C6C}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .spNyl, html code.shiki .spNyl{--shiki-light:#9C3EDA;--shiki-default:#C792EA;--shiki-dark:#C792EA}html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF}html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6